    \field{abstract}{%
    In recent years there have been many successes of using deep
  representations in reinforcement learning. Still, many of these applications
  use conventional architectures, such as convolutional networks, {LSTMs}, or
  auto-encoders. In this paper, we present a new neural network architecture
  for model-free reinforcement learning. Our dueling network represents two
  separate estimators: one for the state value function and one for the
  state-dependent action advantage function. The main benefit of this factoring
  is to generalize learning across actions without imposing any change to the
  underlying reinforcement learning algorithm. Our results show that this
  architecture leads to better policy evaluation in the presence of many
  similar-valued actions. Moreover, the dueling architecture enables our {RL}
  agent to outperform the state-of-the-art on the Atari 2600 domain.%
    }
